# Tackle.io Design & Prototype Execution Spec

**Owner:** Design (Tackle.io, an AppDirect business unit)
**Purpose:** Ensure all generated designs/prototypes are grounded in Tackle.io design tokens and components.
**Primary Design Library (Figma):**
https://www.figma.com/design/b88tCh5B2ujs1KYoJQsvOB/%E2%9A%9B%EF%B8%8F-Tackle-Design-Library?node-id=0-1&t=xpOhyCK3Lrz357je-1

---

## 1) Non-Negotiable Rules

1. **Use only Tackle.io design library tokens and components** from the Figma file above.
2. **Do not invent new visual styles** (color, elevation, spacing, typography, icon style) unless explicitly approved.
3. **Prefer composition over creation:** build new UI by assembling existing components/patterns.
4. **When uncertainty exists, choose an existing component variant** over custom behavior.
5. **"Page - …" pages are composite guidance examples** (not base primitives). Use them to guide page-level structure and patterns.

---

## 2) Token Requirements

Cursor must explicitly use tokens from these library pages:

- `🌈 Color`
- `🌈 Elevation`
- `🌈 Iconography`
- `🌈 Layout & Grid`
- `🌈 Typography`

### 2.1 Color Tokens
- Source: `🌈 Color`
- Use only semantic/system color tokens from the library.
- Avoid hardcoded hex unless directly mapped to a library token.
- Known style examples in file:
  - `Neutral/White`
  - `Neutral/Neutral 10`
  - `NEUTRAL000`
- Verified brand values from tackle.io and downstream.tackle.io:
  - Primary dark navy: `#063649` (`--ast-global-color-0`)
  - Deepest navy: `#002b41` (platform app theme-color)
  - Brand teal: `#1fadad`
  - Logo icon amber: `#FFB600`

### 2.2 Elevation Tokens
- Source: `🌈 Elevation`
- Use defined elevation levels only:
  - `100`
  - `200`
  - `300`
  - `400`
  - `500R`
  - `500L`
- Intent examples:
  - `200`: hover/emphasis/menu overlays
  - `300`: selected cards/rows
  - `400`: alerts/modals/docs tooltips
  - `500R`: right panel/drawer
  - `500L`: left/filter panel

### 2.3 Iconography Tokens
- Source: `🌈 Iconography`
- Use only icon sets and visual treatment from library categories:
  - Warning & Information
  - Tackle Domain
  - Symbols
  - Actions
- Keep icon style, size rhythm, and color mapping aligned to tokenized usage.

### 2.4 Layout & Grid Tokens
- Source: `🌈 Layout & Grid`
- Build page structure with layout primitives:
  - `GlobalHeaderLayout`
  - `PageHeaderLayout`
  - `PageToolbarLayout`
  - `ContentLayout`
  - `LeftPanelLayout`
  - `RightPanelLayout`
  - `Grid` (12-column reference)
- Follow existing spacing and paddings from component/layout variants.

### 2.5 Typography Tokens
- Source: `🌈 Typography`
- Use tokenized text styles only (no ad-hoc font overrides).
- Respect hierarchical usage for page title, section headers, body, helper, labels.
- Known tokenized type set in file: `TextOpenSans` (and typography page guidance).
- Platform app font: **Open Sans** (confirmed in downstream.tackle.io).

