## 4) "Page - …" Composite Guidance Usage

Pages prefixed with **`Page - `** are canonical examples of how to combine components/tokens for real workflows.

Current examples include:
- `Page - Co-Sell List view in Downstream`
- `Page - MSFT Co-Sell Create form in Downstream`

**Rule:** Reuse their composition patterns (header structure, form rhythm, content blocks, action placement) instead of inventing new page architecture.

---

## 5) Cursor Execution Workflow

When generating/updating any design/prototype, Cursor must:

1. Identify target use case and map to closest existing `Page -` composite example.
2. Build skeleton with `Layout & Grid` components first.
3. Populate UI only with approved components above.
4. Apply only library tokens for color/elevation/type/iconography.
5. Validate:
   - No custom visual primitives
   - No hardcoded styles outside token mappings
   - No non-library components
6. Return a concise implementation summary listing:
   - Tokens used
   - Components used
   - Any assumptions/constraints

---

## 6) Quality Gate Checklist (Must Pass)

- [ ] Figma library URL referenced and used as source of truth
- [ ] Only Tackle tokens used (Color, Elevation, Iconography, Layout & Grid, Typography)
- [ ] Only approved components/patterns used
- [ ] Composition aligns to relevant `Page -` examples
- [ ] No ad-hoc styles, one-off shadows, or custom spacing scales
- [ ] Interaction patterns align with component intent (e.g., modal types, menu/button semantics)

